Feature import now preserves GeoJSON features and creates source-linked prisms through `POST /datasets/{id}/process`. Requires site_id, explicit metre heights, class/code/parent metadata and geometry origin. Reprocessing reuses IDs; imports remain UNISSUED until explicit issuance. Use site_id for ambiguous unit codes. Demo reset refuses user-created sites/data. Sample: `data/examples/property_import.geojson`.

Overlap checks mark both conflicting units INVALID regardless of name. Issuance reruns validation. Withdrawing the seeded duplicate preserves history and allows Flat 501 to recover after validation.

External elevation pipeline: raw-byte `POST /datasets/files` accepts bounded LAS/LAZ or DSM/DTM GeoTIFFs with explicit source/vertical metadata. `POST /process/building` uses these datasets and preserves supplied plans; otherwise classical height/footprint estimates create DEGRADED building/floor proposals, with assumptions and source checksums in `GET /runs/{id}`. This is not trained ML or measured apartment segmentation. The synthetic UI action uses `/demo/process/building`. UTILITY LineStrings with explicit constant elevations or depth produce review-required buffered prisms; sloping utilities are rejected.

Run: `docker compose up` at repo root. UI http://localhost:8000. GitHub: tejasva-vardhan/ULPIN-3D

